# Halim Enterprises Limited website: environment variables
#
# Local: copy this file to .env.local and fill in the real values (.env.local is
# gitignored; never commit real values).
# Live:  set the same variables in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment
#        Variables (Production), then redeploy. In Vercel, enter values WITHOUT
#        the surrounding quotes used below.
# Full steps: docs/LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email (contact forms)
#
# The forms send through the Hostinger mailbox info@halimenterpriseslimited.com
# using Nodemailer over SMTP (src/lib/email.ts). Test these settings locally
# with:  npm run email:test   (sends one email to MAIL_TO)
#
# If any of SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, MAIL_FROM or MAIL_TO is
# missing:
#   - in development, nothing is sent and a redacted preview is logged instead;
#   - in production, the forms return 503 with a friendly message.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SMTP server. Confirm in hPanel → Emails → (the mailbox) → Connect apps & devices
SMTP_HOST=smtp.hostinger.com

# 465 for SSL/TLS (recommended), or 587 for STARTTLS
SMTP_PORT=465

# "true" for port 465 (implicit TLS), "false" for 587 (STARTTLS).
# Optional: if left out, it is worked out from the port.
SMTP_SECURE=true

# The mailbox address, and the mailbox's own password (not your hPanel login).
# NEVER commit the password: put it only in .env.local and in Vercel.
SMTP_USER=info@halimenterpriseslimited.com
SMTP_PASS=

# Who the emails come from. The address MUST be the same as SMTP_USER for
# SPF/DKIM alignment (if it isn't, the site sends from SMTP_USER anyway).
# Visitors' addresses only ever go in Reply-To.
MAIL_FROM="Halim Enterprises <info@halimenterpriseslimited.com>"

# Where new enquiries and callback requests are delivered (the business inbox)
MAIL_TO=info@halimenterpriseslimited.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site URL and search engines
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The public address. Every absolute URL uses it: canonical links, og:url,
# sitemap.xml, robots.txt, structured data, the address in emails and the
# forms' Origin check. If unset, it falls back to the same live address
# (src/content/site.ts). Read at build time: redeploy after changing it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.halimenterpriseslimited.com

# Indexing needs no variable: Vercel sets VERCEL_ENV on every deployment.
# Production (VERCEL_ENV=production) is indexed; preview deployments
# (*.vercel.app, VERCEL_ENV=preview) get a site-wide noindex and a robots.txt
# that blocks all crawling. Draft legal pages stay noindexed everywhere while
# site.legal.noindexDraftPages is true.

# Optional: Google Search Console HTML-tag verification. Paste only the
# content="…" value from the meta tag Google gives you. Not needed if you
# verify with a DNS TXT record in Hostinger (the preferred method).
# GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Forms: extra allowed origins (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Extra origins allowed to post to the forms, comma-separated. Not needed for
# the live site or for Vercel preview deployments (their own URL is allowed
# automatically).
# FORM_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com
